  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Decent Work-related SDG indicators mainstreamed in SDGs&apos; national implementation strategy with enhanced institutional capacities in LMIS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Labour Market Information System (LMIS) is pivotal for the development and implementation of efficient employment and labour market-related policies. By aggregating, analyzing, and disseminating labour market data and information, an LMIS provides crucial insights that can guide decision-making processes for governments, employers, job seekers, and educational institutions. 
Recognizing its importance, the ILO in collaboration with GIZ is actively supporting the Ministry of Labour in Jordan in establishing such a system. This initiative is designed to bolster Jordan&apos;s capacity to generate, analyze, and utilize labour market data effectively. The ultimate goal is to inform evidence-based policy development, enhancing the alignment of workforce skills with market demands and ultimately contributing to economic growth and development.
 With funds from the Social Security Corporation (SSC), the ILO will provide technical support in social security policy, financial, actuarial, statistical, legal, administration and project backstopping in line with international labour standards and best international practices. It is hoped this will lead to structural reforms of the social security system in Jordan, including the transition to a multi-tiered system and the adoption of innovative financing approaches to enhance sustainability and coverage.</narrative>
  </description>
